---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout 
  title="Book Repair & Conservation | Kim Baillie"
  description="Archival book repair and paper conservation guides by Kim Baillie. Practical instructions for restoring hardcover and paperback books at book-repair.com."
  ogImage="/images/book-repair.jpg"
>
  <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href="/">Home</a>
    <span class="separator">&rsaquo;</span>
    <span aria-current="page">Book Repair</span>
  </nav>

  <article class="content-box">
    <h1>Book Repair & Conservation</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Books are repositories of knowledge, memories, and personal history. Some years ago, I developed a dedicated online reference site showing book lovers and collectors how to safely preserve and mend cherished volumes.
    </p>

    <div style="margin: 2rem 0; text-align: center;">
      <img src="/images/book-repair.jpg" alt="Book Conservation by Kim Baillie" style="max-width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 8px; box-shadow: var(--shadow);" />
    </div>

    <p>
      The instructions on the website are based on the definitive practical work of Artemis BonaDea (an industry-renowned preservation expert and Alaskan librarian), alongside standard conservation literature by Matt T. Roberts and Don Etherington, combined with my own hands-on workshop experience.
    </p>

    <p>
      Whether you need to tighten a wobbly hardcover hinge, reback a split cloth spine, mend torn pages with reversible wheat starch paste and Japanese tissue, or reinforce paperbacks, you will find clear, step-by-step guides at <strong>book-repair.com</strong>.
    </p>

    <div style="background: #f8fafc; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 8px; padding: 2rem; margin-top: 2.5rem; text-align: center;">
      <h2 style="margin-top: 0; font-family: var(--font-serif); color: var(--text-dark);">Visit How to Repair Your Favourite Books</h2>
      <p style="color: var(--text-muted); max-width: 600px; margin: 0 auto 1.5rem auto;">
        Access over 115 free tutorials, archival tool directories, paper grain testing methods, and bookbinding glossaries.
      </p>
      <a href="https://book-repair.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn" style="max-width: 320px; margin: 0 auto;">
        Visit Book-Repair.com &rarr;
      </a>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
